+    // superman (step 4, 0005): ALPHA-TEST variant of a pixel shader. The Xenos alpha test (RB_COLORCONTROL
+    // alpha_func / alpha_test_enable against RB_ALPHA_REF) runs on oC0.w after the shader, as Xenia's
+    // DxbcShaderTranslator::CompletePixelShader does it (dxbc_shader_translator_om.cc: the LESS / EQUAL / GREATER
+    // mask, NOT_EQUAL as "not equal" so NaN passes, ALWAYS skips, exact compares - use_fuzzy_alpha_epsilon is
+    // false by default). Only a shader that writes colour 0 tests (Xenia: writes_color_target(0)). The host
+    // passes the test in the shared constants: g_AlphaThreshold (c17.x) = RB_ALPHA_REF, g_AlphaTest (c17.y) =
+    // 8 | alpha_func, 0 = no test. Emitted as <hash>.ps.at.dxil; the plain translation is unchanged (the
+    // upstream spec-constant clip stays compiled out in this DXIL build). alphaTestEmitted = the variant holds the
+    // test (the shader writes colour 0).
+    bool alphaTestMode = false;
+    bool alphaTestEmitted = false;
+
     // superman (iter-463): a setTexLOD / UseRegisterLOD fetch needs the
